{#- One item card. Phase 1's Astro <ItemCard> component mirrors this DOM, so the
    class names here are a cross-phase contract, not styling.

    Two columns, and `display:flex` is the whole trick: a client that does not
    understand flex — Outlook — drops both children to block and the card
    stacks vertically, which is exactly the mobile layout. One template, two
    outputs, no second file to keep in sync. Neither float nor table would do
    that. -#}
<article class="uc-card" id="{{ card.anchor }}" data-work-key="{{ card.work_key }}">
  <div class="uc-card__meta">
    {% if card.badges %}
    <p class="uc-card__badges">
      {% for badge in card.badges %}<span class="uc-badge uc-badge--{{ badge.kind }}">{{ badge.label }}</span>{% endfor %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
    {#- The rail is one fact per line: badges, authors, venue, affiliation,
        keywords. Authors and venue were already broken apart; affiliation and
        keywords were not, so the rail ran three facts together on one line.

        **The affiliation line is omitted, not blanked, when there is none.** An
        empty line reads as data we lost rather than data OpenAlex never gave.

        Facet order is `FACET_ORDER` in the code and is not touched here (0j,
        W0-5). -#}
    <p class="uc-card__byline">
      {{ card.authors }}{% if card.authors and card.venue %}<br>{% endif %}{{ card.venue }}
      {%- if card.was_preprint %}<span class="uc-card__was"> · {{ card.was_preprint }}</span>{% endif %}
    </p>
    {% if card.affiliation %}
    <p class="uc-card__affiliation">{{ card.affiliation }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if card.facet_tags %}
    <p class="uc-card__facets">
      {% for tag in card.facet_tags %}<span class="uc-tag" data-entity-id="{{ tag.id }}">{{ tag.label }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}<span class="uc-tag__sep"> · </span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="uc-card__body">
    <h2 class="uc-card__title">
      {%- if card.landing_url %}<a href="{{ card.landing_url }}">{{ card.title }}</a>
      {%- else %}{{ card.title }}{% endif -%}
    </h2>
    {% if card.what %}<p class="uc-card__what">{{ card.what }}</p>{% endif %}
    {#- "Why it matters" and "Caveat" are the template's words. No summary in the
        archive begins with either, checked over all 224 items, so nothing is
        said twice. -#}
    {% if card.why %}
    <p class="uc-card__why"><em class="uc-card__why-lead">Why it matters</em> — {{ card.why }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if card.caveats %}
    <p class="uc-card__caveats"><em>Caveat: {{ card.caveats }}</em></p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if not card.what and not card.why %}
    <p class="uc-card__pending">Summary pending review.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if card.links %}
    <p class="uc-card__links">
      {% for link in card.links %}<a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}<span class="uc-card__link-sep"> · </span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</article>
